# Developer stack lifecycle

Use Ubuntu 24.04 and Bash for every developer command. The canonical checkout
belongs on the Linux filesystem. Windows-only application setup is unsupported.
Do not introduce PowerShell, Windows Node, Docker Desktop, or Windows credential
store dependencies. `dev/equipqr.bat` is only a manual convenience launcher.

```bash
bash dev/linux/dev.sh start
bash dev/linux/dev.sh status
bash dev/linux/dev.sh stop
bash dev/linux/dev.sh reset  # Explicitly erase and reseed the local database
```

Agents may cycle managed services when verification requires it. Stop before
reinstalling dependencies. Restart after app or edge environment changes.
Do not replace managed lifecycle commands with arbitrary process kills or
unrelated container restarts. Startup retains data; reset is an explicit action.

Check app (8080), docs (5174), Auth, and the database-backed Edge health endpoint
before browser verification. Logs live under `tmp/linux-stack/logs`. Process
records include identity checks so stale PIDs do not identify unrelated processes.

All local database operations use the generated Supabase working directory under
`tmp/linux-stack/runtime`. Do not accidentally use a root-level linked project
or start a second Supabase stack. Only one checkout may own these fixed ports.

Codex cloud uses the explicitly approved non-production hosted backend. Setup
installs dependencies; agents start services afterward. Hosted mode never resets
data. Local fixture suites and database tests are local-only.

See [Linux development](../../docs/ops/linux-development.md) for installation,
credentials, verification limits, and the exact Codex settings.
